to create different kinds of blueprints.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.919
But before we do that, let's take a look at

4
00:00:07.919 --> 00:00:10.359
the gameplay framework inside of Unreal Engine.

5
00:00:10.359 --> 00:00:12.279
On this slide, we're looking at some of

6
00:00:12.279 --> 00:00:14.039
the terminology that gets used when

7
00:00:14.039 --> 00:00:17.239
considering the gameplay framework in Unreal Engine.

8
00:00:17.239 --> 00:00:20.120
Some of these key assets we use are a pawn,

9
00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.660
which would be the actor that we are controlling,

10
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:25.000
and that can also be used by AI.

11
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.239
Character would be a subclass or

12
00:00:27.239 --> 00:00:30.940
a child blueprint of a pawn and has additional abilities,

13
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:34.820
like having a skeletal mesh or being able to walk or fly.

14
00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.240
The player controller is the embodiment or

15
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.100
the soul of the player where

16
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.399
input and other data gets processed.

17
00:00:42.399 --> 00:00:45.179
You can actually have your player controller

18
00:00:45.179 --> 00:00:47.280
possessing different characters and

19
00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.340
pawns throughout the same project.

20
00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:51.380
Player state and game state are

21
00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:53.719
more relevant for multiplayer scenarios.

22
00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:56.380
But game mode is one we actually will look at,

23
00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:58.500
and that's where we can actually start to

24
00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.479
define in a particular level

25
00:01:00.479 --> 00:01:04.079
things like the relevant pawn and player controller,

26
00:01:04.079 --> 00:01:07.359
etc, that will be used in that level.

27
00:01:07.359 --> 00:01:11.519
Now that we know what a game mode and a pawn and a character are,

28
00:01:11.519 --> 00:01:15.640
let's look at how we can change what pawn we're using from

29
00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:21.519
the default flying camera to the third-person game mode player.

30
00:01:21.519 --> 00:01:23.640
Here inside of Unreal,

31
00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:30.120
we need to open our World Settings window.

32
00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:34.609
Here we see an option for a game mode override.

33
00:01:34.609 --> 00:01:37.569
It was already imported into this project,

34
00:01:37.569 --> 00:01:38.849
but in case you didn't,

35
00:01:38.849 --> 00:01:43.969
if we come to the Add feature or

36
00:01:43.969 --> 00:01:52.810
content pack and add the third-person character content pack,

37
00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:57.609
we will see here in our drop-down BP third-person game mode.

38
00:01:57.609 --> 00:02:00.890
This sets our default pawn class

39
00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:03.069
to that of the third-person character,

40
00:02:03.069 --> 00:02:06.170
and then these other parts

41
00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:10.729
