42
00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:13.030
But now when we press play,

43
00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:16.830
we will see our third-person character out and about in

44
00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:19.550
the world and we can control them using

45
00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:24.319
a fairly standard WASD space to jump.

46
00:02:24.319 --> 00:02:26.319
We'll notice though that with

47
00:02:26.319 --> 00:02:29.639
our current collision settings on our imported FBX,

48
00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.560
we cannot go on top of it yet,

49
00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.039
so we will look at how we can jump on

50
00:02:35.039 --> 00:02:39.259
that literally in a few more slides.

51
00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:42.090
In the next video,

52
00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:44.490
we'll look at creating an animation blueprint to

